note: Files in steps in a row ("in it", "to it", "the file"), and "file F doesn't exist".
make a new file called "groceries.txt", then write "milk" in it,
then add "eggs" and "bread" to it, one per line, and then show me what's in it.
make a new file called "b.txt", then put "one" in the file, then add "two" to the end of the file,
then show me what's in the file.
if file "nothing.txt" doesn't exist, say "no such file".
if file "b.txt" does not exist, say "wrong".
if folder "missing" doesn't exist:
    say "no folder".
write "old" in file "c.txt".
make a new file called "d.txt", then add "x" to the end of it, then write "y" to it.
say the contents of file "d.txt".
